        <extension point="xbmc.addon.metadata">
            <summary lang="en_GB">PseudoTV Live with M3U/XMLTV live import support.</summary>
            <description lang="en_GB">Fork variant of PseudoTV Live (madteevee) that adds live channel imports from external M3U + XMLTV sources (local files or HTTP URLs) with conflict-cascade allocation and per-channel operator overrides. Designed for parallel install alongside the standard PseudoTV Live addon.</description>
            <platform>all</platform>
            <license>GPL-3.0-or-later</license>
            <source>https://github.com/PseudoTV/PseudoTV_Live</source>
            <forum>https://forum.kodi.tv/showthread.php?tid=355549</forum>
            <disclaimer lang="en_GB">BETA PROJECT; SUBJECT TO BUGS</disclaimer>
            <news>v0.8.0+imports.68
- New: on LiveTV channels the audio language follows the channel too: the language that last played on a channel (your choice or Kodi's) starts it next time, live or replay. A show that lacks that language never changes it.
v0.8.0+imports.67
- Fixed: on LiveTV channels, turning subtitles on or off is remembered per channel. A replay (the RESTART pop-up, the TV guide, or Kodi's automatic next show) and the next live tune start the way you left them on that channel; before, every replay started with subtitles off.
v0.8.0+imports.66
- New: a "Pictures" setting for each imported channel in the web dashboard (Auto / Show / Hide). Hide shows the channel logo in the TV guide instead of the guide's show pictures.
- New: when most of a channel's guide pictures are one same placeholder image (such as an advert), the TV guide shows the channel logo instead. Checked about once a day; one switch per import, on by default.
v0.8.0+imports.62
- New: restart a show that is already running from its beginning (RESTART button after you tune in, TV guide menu, remote button), on your own channels and on Movistar+.</news>
            <reuselanguageinvoker>true</reuselanguageinvoker>
